From: =?utf-8?b?5aSp57+U5aSP6Imy?= <148672659+edi155188son@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:49:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] BD: optional per-cluster post-processing hook in
 BluRayStreamingOptions

Add BluRayStreamingOptions.ClusterPostProcessor (delegate BluRayClusterPostProcessor).
When set, the streaming generator calls it once per 32-sector cluster after the
payload mapping has filled the cluster and before the per-cluster scrambler is
removed, i.e. on the values that end up on the disc. Research tools use it to
solve for LDC parity bytes that land inside a pattern (the parity is GF(2)-linear
in the payload, so free bytes outside the pattern can be adjusted).

The hook is a per-call option, not global state, and is null for every built-in
caller. FillCluster is split into 'fill all sectors' and 'remove scrambler'
loops so the hook sees the complete cluster; with no hook the output bytes and
cancellation points are unchanged.

Test: BluRayParallelGenerationTests flips all bytes in the hook and checks the
output on the sequential and the parallel path, and that the hook runs exactly
once per cluster with the right first sector / PSN.

